Made users and groups as content optional. A site that depends on `pas.plugins.identity:core` alone keeps its users in Plone's own `source_users` and `mutable_properties`: a federated first sign-in creates a `source_users` account with a random password nobody knows, which does not count as a way in when unlinking the last identity, and writes the provider's name and first offered address to the member's properties. The provider's property map is applied to empty properties on every sign-in, writing text only: a number becomes text, a list, an object or a boolean is not written, and a value a property refuses is logged and skipped rather than failing the sign-in. Group maps write to `source_groups`, and an identity whose account was deleted gets it back. Before, such a sign-in answered HTTP 500. On these sites the Identity providers control panel leaves out the Profile settings, the Profile entry of the user menu opens Volto's personal information form, and exporting or importing principals is refused with a message naming the `contenttypes` profile. Which kind of site it is comes from the new `IUsersAsContent` marker on the site root, which the `contenttypes` profile sets and its uninstall removes. @ericof
